  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="feed-reshare-content__commentary">I just published a 4-part series on Google Cloud medium exploring how <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/googlemapsplatform/?trk=public_post_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="public_post_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Google Maps Platform</a> prevents AI agents from making expensive real-world mistakes:
<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Flnkd%2Ein%2FeFgSk9uM&amp;urlhash=d9Cc&amp;trk=public_post_reshare-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="public_post_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/eFgSk9uM</a>

The inspiration? <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/andonlabs?trk=public_post_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="public_post_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Andon Labs</a> Vending-Bench (2025) gave AI models like Claude and GPT-4 a simple task: run a vending machine. They failed spectacularly—believing deliveries arrived when trucks were hours away, threatening FBI intervention over $2 fees 🤣 , ordering 500 tungsten cubes after confusing memes for market demand.

The lesson: AI excels at language but can't maintain coherent understanding of physical reality over time.

This matters for local service businesses. The photo shows what happens when AI specifies reclaimed teak flooring without knowing the building has 85°F radiant heating.  Result: $25,000 in cracked wood.

My series shows how Google Maps APIs ground AI in reality:
-Routes API verifies actual delivery arrival
-Solar &amp; Aerial View APIs reveal site constraints
-Vector Search + Gemini digitizes physical samples
-Orchestration creates self-correcting feedback loops

We're building systems that understand the difference between what's possible in language and what's possible in physics.

If a vending machine AI loses $1 on imaginary candy bars, that's research. When it can lose $25K on flooring, that's a problem! 🙀</p>
<!---->  </div>



        
      
    
    
    

