  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Inferentia2 is dedicated hardware for running inference native to the AWS stack.  Each inf2 chip has 16 GB dedicated fast memory and they are bundled as a unit of 2 chips- for 32 GB memory.

Gemma4 is Google's open source model.  The key change with Gemma4 is that the model weights are fully open source licensed under Apache2.

Gemma4 has some advanced techniques for managing the model and ports to Inf2 hardware have struggled.  

I took a deep dive with a full suite of Python MCP DevOps tools to port Gemma4 to Inf2.  

Why?  The Inf2 processors offer excellent price performance and offer significant savings especially when you can run your workload as spot.

It also turned out to be more of a DevOps problem than you would expect beyond the model porting issues.  

To build and manage the Deployments, run the Neuron compiler, and build the Docker files required careful management of the EC2 instances.

AWS Builder Center article is here:
<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Flnkd%2Ein%2FgUAiBJ-j&amp;urlhash=F8we&amp;trk=public_post-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="public_post-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gUAiBJ-j</a>

Medium is here:
<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Flnkd%2Ein%2FggJ7ikFQ&amp;urlhash=41KF&amp;trk=public_post-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="public_post-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/ggJ7ikFQ</a>

<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=http%3A%2F%2Fdev%2Eto&amp;urlhash=zTdX&amp;trk=public_post-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="public_post-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>dev.to</a> is here:
<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Flnkd%2Ein%2FgfSuQm7E&amp;urlhash=Nucr&amp;trk=public_post-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="public_post-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gfSuQm7E</a>


