  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Google has a lot of products and tech across the whole stack.  From TPUS, to LLMs, to complex multi-cluster orchestration.  

It is easy to miss something with so many products.

Gemma4 is one of the Hidden Gems of the whole Google Stack.  The weights for model family are available under an Apache2 license.  

So what does that mean?  You are free to slice/ dice/ sautee/ redistribute/ whatever with the complete set of weights across the entire family.

Do you want to see how the 2B mixed head KV cache works?  Pull them and run them.  Don't take my word or Claude's word for it!

This article moves way down the stack to almost the hardware level and explores running a straight JAX version of Gemma 2B directly on TPU hardware.  It is not going to replace vLLM anytime soon.

The real benefit from this project was the approaches and practical MLOPS.  How do you optimize your startup?  How long does it take to run a test to validate a change?  How much can you automate?  

There are still tons of open questions.

Article is here:
